ails only modestly but cannot close the gap"], "rationale": "Every independent poll since early October shows Hochul ahead by 9 to 18 points, averaging around 13, and all eight expert raters place the race at Likely D or better. Markets at 96-97% and surging NYC early voting reinforce a Safe D call.", "watch": "A late polling error of several points toward Republicans, as seen in some past New York races, would narrow the margin but is unlikely to flip the outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Kathy Hochul (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Kathy Hochul seeks a full term as New York governor against Nassau County Executive Bruce Blakeman. Polling has been remarkably steady: independent surveys from Siena, Quinnipiac, Marist, Emerson and others all show Hochul up by roughly 9 to 18 points, with the aggregate near 13. Even Republican-sponsored polls show her ahead, though by smaller margins. Fundraising is roughly comparable, with Hochul holding a slight cash edge, but money has not changed the race's shape.\n\nExpert raters uniformly place the race at Likely D or better, and prediction markets price Hochul's chances at 96 to 97 percent. New York's Democratic lean, incumbency advantages, and heavy early voting in New York City all point the same direction. Blakeman needs a historic polling miss to contend; the realistic question is the size of the margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9776, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9779, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9761, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9756, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9778, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9796, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "